**Read:** [Metals, alloys, steels, and graduate modeling — Bhadeshia teaching materials](../../../materials/metals-and-metallurgical-production/sources/Metals-Alloys-and-Graduate-Teaching-Bhadeshia.lingua#r_0HZJKN8WC6SEWA0DABM8P4HC3F), the full phase-transformation and heat-treatment teaching material; [Phase Transitions — Bhadeshia and Yan](../../../materials/metals-and-metallurgical-production/sources/Phase-Transitions-Bhadeshia-Yan.lingua#r_2PMPJ2B4GPGDT62S567TX1DCPJ), the relevant diffusion, nucleation/growth and transformation treatments; [Materials kinetics — MIT 3.205 and 3.21](../sources/Kinetic-Processes-in-Materials-MIT.lingua#r_2BZVQ9NG9Y2XTF4QG0H3JYYS16), transformation and restoration problems. Return to the earlier alloy-state, precipitation, recovery and thermal-mismatch Records.

A thermal cycle aims at a specified structure, not merely a furnace setpoint. Solution treatment, annealing, quenching, tempering and aging have different purposes and material-dependent limits. Heating and cooling gradients interact with phase changes, plasticity and restraint. A surface temperature can miss a delayed interior transformation, while a nominally uniform final hardness can conceal different residual stresses or phase distributions.

**Work:** Reconstruct a transformed steel and a precipitation-strengthened alloy from their initial states through measured thermal histories and final evidence. Derive a heat-transfer estimate, a transformation/aging account and a dimensional or stress consequence. Compare a faster schedule with a slower one through grain/precipitate state, retained phases, distortion and useful response. Explain which observations distinguish incomplete transformation, overaging and quench damage. Carry atmosphere, section size and subsequent machining into the account.

**Return:** [Materials engineering — structure, processing and useful behavior](../Materials-engineering.lingua#r_05BF5JM8141RKF1VT5998YFZQ9).
**Continue in materials engineering:** [Machining, finishing and the altered surface layer](Machining-finishing-and-the-altered-surface-layer.lingua#r_6509Q6WA6W909JZGHG4ESZ069B).

